speechtext:
The new amendments have been placed in their proper order as they should be finally in the act. Consequently clause 2 of the bill before the committee reads, "recorded on medical examination prior to enlistment." It is intended to define that phrase, "recorded on medical examination prior
to enlistment". I will ask my colleague the Minister of Public Works (Mr. Fournier) to move the following amendment:
Section two of the said act is further amended by adding thereto, immediately after paragraph (nn) thereof, the following paragraph:
(nnm) "recorded on medical examination prior to enlistment" includes recorded symptoms or findings ini,
(i)	medical proceedings for enlistment;
(ii)	official documentation covering any former period of service;
(iii)	the files of the department;
(iv)	compensation board or insurance company records;
(v)	hospital, private physician or other medical authority,
where such record refers to the injury or disease resulting in the disability in respect of which the application for pension is made;

Mr. Speaker, may I interject. My hon. friend has been deliberately comparing rentals of unheated, single dwellings with rentals of fully heated and fully serviced apartments. He might as well compare the cost of a piano with the cost of a sewing machine. The two are wholly unrelated. Now he is going to give the incomes of 1942 and relate them to building costs in 1948. He can do that if he likes;
National Housing Act

but if he thinks he is deceiving anyone, certainly he will not deceive anyone in this house.
